## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

**Chủ đề: idempotency — từ điện thoại đến ràng buộc database.**

> *"Idempotency means doing something twice has the same effect as doing it once. It matters for mobile more than for web, because phones lose connectivity mid-request. The user taps save, the request goes out, the network drops before the response comes back. The app doesn't know whether it worked, so it retries — and now you might have two records.*
> *I solved this in two layers. On the client, the app generates a UUID for each meal before sending, so a retry carries the same ID. On the server, there's a unique constraint on user ID plus client ID, and the insert uses ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE.*
> *The reason I need both: the client-generated ID makes retries identifiable, but only the database constraint actually guarantees uniqueness. Application logic can have bugs — two requests can race past a check. The constraint can't be raced.*
> *I built the client half in October and the server half today, which is the first time I've seen a whole problem from both ends."*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `mid-request` | giữa lúc request đang chạy | *The network drops mid-request.* |
| `race past a check` | hai luồng vượt qua kiểm tra cùng lúc | *Two requests can race past a check.* |
| `guarantee` (v) | đảm bảo chắc chắn | *Only the constraint guarantees it.* |
| `identifiable` | nhận dạng được | *The client ID makes retries identifiable.* |
| `from both ends` | từ cả hai phía | *I've seen the problem from both ends.* |

